-- A performed `alloc` is a fresh cell serviced from an arena, cheaper but not
-- absent, so an `@ noalloc` function that performs it is rejected exactly like
-- one that builds a fresh constructor: arenas and the allocation certificate
-- stay orthogonal and honest. The operation is imported rather than redeclared:
-- an operation belongs to the module that declares it, so only the real
-- `Arena.alloc` carries this meaning and a lookalike of the same bare name is
-- an ordinary effect the certificate says nothing about.
import Arena

fn grab(n : Int) : Arena.Cell @ noalloc ! {Arena.Alloc} = Arena.alloc(n)
